{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1358085-is-there-more-information-on-the-legion-of-silence","id":1358085,"title":"Is there more information on the Legion of Silence?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-31T14:35:22-08:00","id":1358085,"title":"Is there more information on the Legion of Silence?","content":"I had an idea for a new character and wanted to see if it works within the setting.<br /> <br /> Specifically, I am interested in a member being trained/groomed for the Legion of Silence Exalting as a Dragon-Blooded. I can find only limited information in the Realm or Dragon-Blooded Books (3E) and don't have access to my 1E or 2E books that might have more information on the Legion of Silence... specifically if those who are groomed/trained to be part of this group can even Exalt as Dragon-Bloods. With the information I have at my disposal, I see no real reason why they couldn't... though the sorceries involved might prevent it.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of the character being a silent giant of a warrior dedicated to protecting his band-mates. I know that this doesn't have to mean that the character was originally going to be part of the Legion of Silence before he Exalted and was sent to be trained with other Lost Eggs found in the Realm, but the idea does have some additional appeal too. Just wanted to see if there is any setting information people might know of from previous editions that might make this either difficult (rare) or impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T15:13:45-08:00","id":1358090,"title":"","content":"You are very much in luck my friend, in The Realm, the 3e book, there IS a legionnaire who exalted as a DB and decided to go live as a silent monk. She's on page 129 of that book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T21:41:22-08:00","id":1358142,"title":"","content":"Well... that works out well for the character I am creating.<br /> <br /> Of course this does present a couple of minor problems that I hadn't thought of until now... such as how to represent the character communicating with hand gestures... Exalted doesn't exactly have a sign language (at least I didn't see one listed in the book). I had thought of using performance and the charms there in to help with communication in a manner similar to how the faun/satyr character of Toot from the old Hercules cartoon from the 70s (iifc) communicated with the centaur Newton (and sometimes Herc... this was the cartoon where his strength came from a ring he wore and for some reason kept in his belt rather than on his finger at all times like most people do). Not sure if that would work though... have to see how much can be communicated with the use of the non singing charms.<br /> <br /> Regardless, while this character will have gone through the process that contributes to the extraordinary size of the Legion of Silence, he didn't complete the training before Exalting as a Dragon-Blood. His new status as a Prince of the Earth meant that he would be transferred to the Splendid and Just Arbiters of Purpose where he would get the basic training that all Dragon-Bloods not born in the Dynasty (Great Houses or patrician families) before deciding between the Razor and the Coin. In this character's case, he chose the Coin and attended Pasiap's Stair. His size and strength allowed him to excel at the rigorous training there, but also develop greater dexterity than many would think someone so big could be while honing his mind as well (mostly in war tactics of course). In the end, he was able to graduate impressively (well above the average, though given the elite group he would have been a part of had he not Exalted, this wasn't unexpected). After this, he joined the Legions as a low ranked officer (his muteness might be a hindrance here, but I could have him assigned as the personal guard of a more senior officer).<br /> <br /> I do have one other question when it comes to Lost Eggs that attend Pasiap's Stairs... would they get the 5 bonus merits that Dynasts, Lookshians and those from Prasad would? They are technically still from the Realm, though not part of the Dynasty. I am inclined to say yes, as they do attend one of the Realm's Academies (albeit, one meant for those outside the Great Houses), even if they don't have an influential Greater House backing them. Such Outcastes may not be part of the Dynasty, but they should still have some benefit from being from the Realm, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T21:54:34-08:00","id":1358144,"title":"","content":"Silent Legionaire merits are covered on page 80 of The Realm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T02:03:59-08:00","id":1358160,"title":"","content":"My ruling in my game was &quot;yes to Dynastic merit points&quot;.<br /> <br /> Being Mute is a Flaw. Everyone who shares a common language with you understands your gesturing without a roll... unless you want +2 Dragon Experience from them not understanding you at a dramatic point that session. Social Influence rolls give +2 Resolve to your target.<br /> <br /> Performance Charms are a good idea. You might want to look at the higher Essence Linguistics Charms too.<br /> <br /> Alternatively buy sign language as a Tribal Language.<br /> <br /> I see such an obviously gifted warrior leading a kind of Spec Ops team -- moving in silence, coordinating with hand signels. A kind of reaver vanguard for the Legion. Love the idea of being an attach\u00e9 to a more senior officer (Mentor oppertunity right there).<br /> <br /> As they're not a full member of the Legion of Silence, I'd be dubious about giving them the full LoS Merit package in the Realm. I'd probably stick with Giant and maybe Unspeaking.<br /> <br /> Very cool idea. Hope your game goes well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T10:01:46-08:00","id":1358218,"title":"","content":"Probably go with the Powerful Grasp merit too... but the Imperial Devotion doesn't seem to fit the character as his background says he didn't complete the full training though his body did receive the alterations. Now that I have a better grasp on who this character Is, I can go back and readjust the skills, merits and charm selections to better reflect this.<br /> <br /> Also, I tend to design characters both as a young Dragon-Blood just before they attend Secondary School (Essence 1) and then upgrade them to what they would be as a standard Dragon-Blood that is newly graduated (which is the default assumption for the standard character creation rules in WFHW).<br /> <br /> I am looking forward to the companion book (Heirs to the Shogunate iirc) for the new charms and other options that might be included (especially new information on Dragon-Bloods outside the Realm. Hoping there are new merits as well, since there were very few (2) in WFHW. Of course I should have more than enough to make this character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T12:56:56-08:00","id":1358233,"title":"","content":"I have to admit that I am both pleased and surprised that there far more information on the Legion of Silence in 3E than the brief write-up in the Legion section of The Realm book... and that it does provide me much of what I need for the character concept I was going for. I thought that I would have to get setting information from previous editions that may or may not have relevance to 3E.<br /> <br /> Thank you DrLoveMonkey for showing me where a Silent Legionnaire that had Exalted could be found and to Lioness for showing me the write-up that included some unique merits common among the Legion of Silence. These sources will be changing the character I originally was going to settle with to be more like how I envision him to be. I will still have to make a few concessions due to the mechanical limitations of character generation, but I should have a good framework to build upon as the character develops past this point.<br /> <br /> If there is enough interest, I may even present the character here once I have it completed... including a brief background for the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}